The package builds offline with the `go-mod/` source component from the
companion `hyprmoncfg-<version>-deps.tar.xz` release asset. During package
builds, `debian/rules` moves that cache next to the unpacked source tree so
`go test ./...` does not recurse into cached modules.

Official Debian inclusion may require replacing this cache with packaged Go
dependencies. Treat this packaging as a public, buildable starting point, not
as a final Debian policy decision.

To build the binary package from the `debian/sid` branch, download the matching
dependency archive next to the checkout, unpack it into the checkout, and run:

  tar -xf ../hyprmoncfg-@VERSION@-deps.tar.xz
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

The resulting package is written to the parent directory.
